  `mixes_in` — IMPLEMENTED at R3 without a grammar change: the heritage expression's SHAPE
  (a call in extends position) is the discriminator, and the whole-population construct
  census counts 2 such sites while the analyzer publishes 2 `mixes_in` edges.
  `part_of` — IMPLEMENTED at R2 by patching the pinned grammar so the directive is a
  `reference_directive` NODE (the stock grammar lexes it as a comment, which the A2/A3
  halves above still show — that is why the patch was needed), proven behaviourally by
  script/m14/ts-partof-grammar-proof.ts (8/8 green) and served via the engine digest table;
  the construct census counts 50 directive sites vs 49 published rows (one repeated triple).
  ⇒ n = 14 of 14, and this instrument remains the citation for WHY the stock grammar could
    not carry the `part_of` construct without the patch, and why `mixes_in` needs no node.
